course: everyday
lesson: 423
title: Older siblings and YouTube gameplay
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Theo's brother Marcus is seventeen and plays GTA 6 in the living room. Theo used to sit on the arm of the sofa, «just watching». Then one night Theo couldn't sleep, because a scene he had watched kept playing in his head with the lights off. Marcus felt awful when he found out. Now he plays it when Theo is in bed, and on Saturdays they play a racing game together, where Marcus loses on purpose about once a month and pretends it was an accident. Theo knows. He lets him pretend.
explain: Priya's sister plays GTA in the bedroom and says: «Don't tell Mum.» Zara's brother offers to let her play when their parents are out. Both girls felt the same squeeze: wanting to be one of the big kids, and not wanting to get the big kid into trouble. Zara said: «Nah, I'll just get nightmares and you'll get grounded. Bad deal.» Her brother laughed and played cards with her instead. Priya kept the secret for a week, felt sick about it, then told her mum, who talked to the sister calmly, and nobody was grounded for ever.
explain: Kai watched GTA 6 gameplay on YouTube without asking, and then the trouble started: YouTube kept showing him more and more of it, each video louder and nastier than the last, because the app shows you more of whatever you click. Ollie had the same thing after one video. Noah's favourite gaming YouTuber swears so much that his little sister started saying «absolutely ****ing brilliant» at the breakfast table, which went down badly with Grandma.
explain: Some videos are great. Mia found a YouTuber who plays kids' games and is honestly funny: he falls off ladders in Minecraft and screams like a kettle. Ruby's older sister, now nineteen, told her she waited until eighteen to play GTA, «and it was actually better, because I got the jokes and the story, not just the shooting». Jayden's brother plays GTA online with grown-up strangers, and Jayden learned the most useful rule of all from him: «If a stranger online asks how old you are or where you live, I log off. You should too.»
fact: Watching a game being played can be just as frightening or upsetting as playing it yourself.
fact: The age rating of a game also applies to watching other people play it.
fact: Video apps show you more of whatever you click, so one video can quickly fill your list with similar ones.
fact: A grown-up can help clear your watch history, so the app stops filling your list with the same kind of video.
fact: If something you watched keeps scaring you, talking about it with a grown-up helps.
fact: Many gaming YouTubers make videos for grown-ups, with strong swearing and violent games.
fact: YouTube's own rules say children under 13 should use YouTube Kids or a supervised account.
fact: A secret that makes you feel sick or scared is a secret worth telling a trusted grown-up.
fact: Older siblings often want to be kind but forget how younger children feel about scary scenes.
fact: Online games for grown-ups are full of grown-up strangers whom you know nothing about.
fact: Nobody online needs your age, your school or your address, so it is safest never to share them.
fact: Saying no to a big kid's offer can be done kindly, and suggesting something else to do together helps.
exercise: Why could Theo not sleep after «just watching»? | A scene he watched kept playing in his head | The sofa was too uncomfortable to sit on | His brother was playing too loudly all night | He was angry that he could not play himself
exercise: What did Marcus change after he found out? | He plays GTA after Theo is in bed | He gave the game away to a friend | He made Theo play it with him | He stopped speaking to Theo for a week
exercise: Why does Theo let Marcus pretend his losses are accidents? | It is Marcus's kind way of being a good brother | Theo really believes they are all just accidents | Theo wants Marcus to stay embarrassed | Theo does not care who wins the race
exercise: What «squeeze» did Priya and Zara both feel? | Wanting to join the big kids, not wanting to get them in trouble | Wanting to play the game, but not knowing how all the buttons work | Wanting to sleep, but not being tired enough yet | Wanting to watch TV, but the TV being broken
exercise: Why did Zara call her brother's offer a «bad deal»? | She'd get nightmares and he'd get grounded | She thought the game was far too easy for her | She wanted to play a different 18 game | She had too much homework to play
exercise: How did Priya feel while keeping her sister's secret? | Sick and uneasy about it | Proud and happy about it all | Bored and a bit sleepy about it | Calm and quite certain about it
exercise: What happened after Priya told her mum? | Mum talked to the sister calmly | Her sister was grounded for a year | Her mum bought GTA for both girls | Nobody ever spoke about it again
exercise: Why did YouTube keep showing Kai more GTA videos? | The app shows more of whatever you click | YouTube shows GTA to every child | His friends sent the videos to him | GTA pays YouTube to show it to children like Kai
exercise: What happened because of Noah's swearing YouTuber? | His little sister copied the words at breakfast | Noah won a prize for the funniest video | Grandma started watching the YouTuber every day too | Noah's sister became a YouTuber herself
exercise: What made Mia's YouTuber a good choice? | He plays kids' games and is really funny | He swears in a very funny voice | He plays only games rated 18 | He has the most viewers in the world
exercise: Why did Ruby's sister think waiting until 18 was better? | She understood the jokes and the story | The game was much cheaper by the time she was 18 | She was better at shooting by then | Her friends had all stopped playing
exercise: What rule did Jayden learn from his brother? | Log off if a stranger asks your age or address | Always tell strangers you are a grown-up | Only play with strangers who seem friendly | Give your school's name but not your street
exercise: Why are online games for grown-ups risky for a child? | They are full of grown-up strangers | They make consoles break down more often | The internet is much slower for children | They cost more money for younger players
exercise: Does the age rating of a game matter when you only watch it? | Yes, watching can upset you just as much | No, ratings only count when you hold the controller | No, watching is always safe for any age | Yes, but only if you watch for over an hour
exercise: Which kind of courage did Priya show in the end? | Telling the truth even though it was uncomfortable | Keeping the secret no matter what happened to anyone | Playing the game to prove she was big | Shouting at her sister in front of Mum
exercise: What could Kai do to stop the GTA videos filling his list? | Ask a grown-up to help clear his history | Watch every GTA video until they run out | Click on even more of them to finish them | Leave the videos playing with the sound off
test: «I'm not playing it, just watching, so it's fine innit». Is that right? | No, watching can upset you as much as playing | Yes, ratings are only for players | Yes, if you watch from the other room | No, watching is worse than playing it
test: Big sis: «don't tell mum ok?? or I'm dead». Priya feels sick. What's wise? | Tell a trusted grown-up, the secret is bothering her | Keep it forever, to be a good and loyal sister to her | Play the game too so they're equal | Tell the whole class instead of Mum
test: Zara's bro: «parents out tonight, wanna play GTA?» Which reply is wise and kind? | Nah, nightmares for me, trouble for you, cards? | Yes, but only the scary bits, quickly | Only if you pay me five pounds first | Yes, and I won't tell them, promise
test: Kai watched one GTA vid, now his whole YouTube is GTA. Why? | The app shows more of what you click | His tablet has a virus from the video | Someone hacked his account last night | YouTube only has GTA videos now
test: Noah's little sis at breakfast, copying the YouTuber: a big swear word. Grandma's face! What's the lesson? | Little kids copy what they hear in videos | Grandma should watch the YouTuber too | Swearing is fine if a famous YouTuber says it | Breakfast is the wrong time for videos
test: Random in online game: «how old r u, which school u go to?» What should Jayden do? | Log off and tell a grown-up | Tell him, he seems friendly enough | Say a different school as a joke | Ask him his age and school first
test: Marcus: «sorry mate, didn't know it'd give you nightmares». What does this show about Marcus? | He cares and didn't realise how Theo felt | He wanted Theo to have nightmares | He thinks Theo is making it up | He doesn't like playing with Theo
test: Ruby: «why did you wait till 18 for GTA?» Sister: «...» What did she say? | I got the jokes and story, not just shooting | It was too hard to play when I was little | Mum had hidden it in the attic for years | The game wasn't invented before I was 18
test: Mia: «this guy fell off a ladder and screamed like a kettle lol». What kind of video is this? | A funny video of a kids' game | A scary video of a game rated 18 | A video teaching kids how to cheat | A sad video about broken ladders
test: Which age does YouTube say you should be to have your own normal account? | 13 or older | 7 or older | 10 or older | 18 or older
test: Theo watched the scary bit, now he can't sleep. What helps most? | Telling a grown-up and talking about it | Watching it again to get used to it | Keeping quiet so Marcus isn't in trouble | Playing the game himself the next day
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the applicability of an age rating to the viewing of gameplay by a child? | The rating remains relevant, viewing being capable of causing distress | The rating ceases to apply where the child does not play | The rating applies solely to the purchaser of the game | The rating is applicable only during school hours
exam: Identify the principal reason for which a video platform persists in recommending content resembling that which a user has previously selected. | The platform recommends further material similar to prior selections | The platform is obliged by law to repeat each video | The user's device has been compromised by a harmful program | The content is recommended equally to every user
exam: It is given that a child is requested by a sibling to conceal conduct which occasions the child distress. Select the response consistent with sound guidance. | The matter ought to be disclosed to a trusted adult | The secret ought to be maintained in all circumstances | The child ought to participate in the conduct concerned | The matter ought to be disclosed to classmates
exam: Determine the most prudent course of action where an unknown participant in an online game requests a child's age and place of residence. | To disconnect and inform a responsible adult | To supply the information with courtesy | To supply false information in jest | To request the participant's details in return
